       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** 4000 mg four times daily, which is 16,000 mg/day.\n- **Maximum for ibuprofen:** the usual limit is 3200 mg/day for adults in a monitored setting, and 1200 mg/day for OTC use. A single dose is typically 400\u2013800 mg.\n\nThe order is five times the maximum daily dose. That puts the patient at serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and other toxicity.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2400 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2400 mg/day)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If 4000 mg was intended, please confirm that with your supervising resident or attending, and I can enter it with a note recording that."
